osdlib.h uses std::uint8_t and std::size_t but includes neither <cstdint> nor
<cstddef>; it only worked because some other header happened to drag them in
transitively.  GCC 13 tightened its libstdc++ include graph, so the transitive
path is gone and the header no longer compiles:

  osdlib.h:111:68: error: 'uint8_t' in namespace 'std' does not name a type

Include what is used.  Unrelated to cross-compiling -- this breaks on any
GCC 13 host too.

--- a/src/osd/modules/lib/osdlib.h
+++ b/src/osd/modules/lib/osdlib.h
@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@
 #ifndef __OSDLIB__
 #define __OSDLIB__
 
+#include <cstddef>
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <initializer_list>
 #include <string>
 #include <type_traits>
